      ],
      "conceptFormula": "To solve $ax + b = c$:\n1. Apply Subtraction Property of Equality: $ax = c - b$\n2. Apply Division Property of Equality: $x = \\frac{c - b}{a}$",
      "steps": [
        {
          "stepNumber": 1,
          "title": "Subtract 5 from both sides",
          "calculation": "$$2x = 17 - 5 = 12$$",
          "explanation": "Subtracting the constant term isolates the term containing $x$."
        },
        {
          "stepNumber": 2,
          "title": "Divide both sides by 2",
          "calculation": "$$x = \\frac{12}{2} = 6$$",
          "explanation": "Dividing by the coefficient of $x$ gives the value of $x$."
        }
      ],
      "finalAnswer": "$$x = 6$$",
      "verification": "Substitute $x = 6$ into the original LHS:\n$$LHS = 2(6) + 5 = 12 + 5 = 17 = RHS$$\nThe equation balances, confirming the solution!",
      "learningTip": "Whatever operation you perform on the left-hand side, you must perform identically on the right-hand side to keep the equation balanced.",
      "methods": [
        {
          "name": "Standard Algebraic Balancing",
          "description": "Step-by-step inverse operations"
        },
